  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_cf804410309544d79401b6afb076ff65",
      "statement": "The sandbox is created via `Sandbox.create` without any `source` argument, and the repo is manually cloned inside the sandbox to `/vercel/sandbox/project` with `git clone --depth 1 <authenticatedUrl>`; the authenticated URL embeds the GitHub token as username and `x-oauth-basic` as password for `github.com` URLs only.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/commands.ts#L1-L4",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8bd490d8140964e9412e640e0fe98b8bbb9d59c529969393ce80673d8d7e4d39:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/config.ts#L69-L86",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:94f8b47bdd50dd04ff13bee78e93b34f8c1f32b3fe330111702a3d0ed7d3a441:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/creation.ts#L82-L132",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:adb13c049f73228064d1b4ed7d9ef0a5ef81fef99e8cc27a425a70d3f46117ce:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bc990faa35614764b31d65a9f54d9930",
      "statement": "The `timeout` argument passed to `Sandbox.create` is computed solely from `maxDuration * 60_000` ms (with `maxDuration` resolved from `task.maxDuration` then `getMaxSandboxDuration(userId)` then `MAX_SANDBOX_DURATION`); the `keepAlive` flag plays no role in this calculation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/%5BtaskId%5D/start-sandbox/route.ts#L80-L108",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:149b146fee270d348aff5af0dc9a6fb31a15719dfa12885b7f2844663d5126e2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/db/settings.ts#L69-L72",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dab56cca2306b7962dce9709e275c854be02476f80440280209a848728ef416c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/creation.ts#L73-L90",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4e53340a4f13779fdc35d28d7de00204bd770beec716ae5f58edd1a75b4e2da3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_43167cb515a343c5806cf0f03682ac30",
      "statement": "The `keepAlive` flag has exactly one operational effect: it controls whether the worker calls `unregisterSandbox(taskId)` and the best-effort `shutdownSandbox(sandbox)` after the agent run completes (and on error). It does not extend the SDK-side sandbox lifetime.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/%5BtaskId%5D/continue/route.ts#L398-L453",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:476534d125fae7d1857e75e1342928d5f037667c5b49abc66b449b50d95331a1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/route.ts#L668-L727",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d2399b17691f39764cb8343a9a6c0064025b98e6bfc453a72954028c7ac8a48:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/creation.ts#L73-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ee788b85362109ad2e95434abc8ea87659292e48299cd80c42ac848541c7001b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bb043e0e89904bb89a3f5538297085ea",
      "statement": "`createSandbox` calls `registerSandbox(taskId, sandbox, keepAlive)` immediately after `Sandbox.create` returns successfully and before any further work (clone, dependency install, dev server), so the in-memory registry always has a live reference for any later `killSandbox(taskId)` call.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/creation.ts#L97-L109",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:698e3ec3f3ef0d240c0e452b7f5cb67aa65daa4f500baba2d947608ba89e07c4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/sandbox-registry.ts#L11-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f3fa22d508c8020908b752b800e380d3d079b60a035630ab56a2ce7480089ebc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0a66cfb7ff5c4015be38842fbc82a8a2",
      "statement": "Sandbox reachability is split between two stores with different lifetimes: an in-memory `Map<taskId, Sandbox>` (`lib/sandbox/sandbox-registry.ts`, valid for a single serverless execution) and the persistent `tasks.sandboxId` + `tasks.sandboxUrl` text columns on the `tasks` row (`lib/db/schema.ts`). The two are written together after `createSandbox` returns and cleared together on `keepAlive=false` shutdown.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/route.ts#L518-L518",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9436a45c1c29d81726efefad341d5cce205cf997e69d8549e905c222d629c14b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/db/schema.ts#L99-L101",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c7e31008c65b57e56811f93c29b16fc08a14e0d942e4ad90c479484b400427a8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/sandbox-registry.ts#L9-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:903a9ed65a3c6537a8f4b3ebcc39f36a0f57ec32cae1a9bc6d7f8a372436a62a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0b3bd06244af4006a264939d241c1010",
      "statement": "Cross-request reconnect is performed via `Sandbox.get({ sandboxId, teamId, projectId, token })` reading `tasks.sandboxId` and the three `SANDBOX_VERCEL_*` env vars; every endpoint that needs the sandbox outside the original worker (continue, terminal, file ops, sandbox-health, restart-dev, merge-pr, stop-sandbox, etc.) follows this pattern.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/%5BtaskId%5D/continue/route.ts#L169-L190",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cdc24e4d10e0d7145c298bc4eb4a2b7a6447ae9e980b9081c5995c898d5256fb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/%5BtaskId%5D/sandbox-health/route.ts#L40-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:715496734eacb50dd1a14ae0991434470569a2d699474242ded48e42d011a7e5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/%5BtaskId%5D/terminal/route.ts#L42-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8edc193ba63b620de05e8d08da8db86c000dad7672ad5234c2ce2d00f21f2a3a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_394d385e154b49a3856b690b5cb1cbc2",
      "statement": "The canonical reconnect preamble in API route handlers is `getSandbox(taskId) ?? await Sandbox.get({ sandboxId, teamId, projectId, token })` — consulting the in-memory map first as a fast path and falling back to `Sandbox.get()` when the map no longer has the reference (cross-execution).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/%5BtaskId%5D/terminal/route.ts#L42-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8edc193ba63b620de05e8d08da8db86c000dad7672ad5234c2ce2d00f21f2a3a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/sandbox-registry.ts#L21-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3effc4ec922fbee044dee46f5833eab4944ed36edb66c0b6d1d90ab0aa52d84f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8832eb91c0f2437683b05e5320e92a6c",
      "statement": "Three shutdown paths exist with non-interchangeable semantics: (A) the worker's success/error branches call `unregisterSandbox + shutdownSandbox` (best-effort `pkill` of node/python/npm/yarn/pnpm, no SDK stop); (B) `POST /api/tasks/:taskId/stop-sandbox` reconnects via `Sandbox.get` and calls SDK `sandbox.stop()` then clears the DB columns; (C) `POST /api/tasks/:taskId/merge-pr` does the same after a successful merge and ignores `keepAlive`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/%5BtaskId%5D/merge-pr/route.ts#L57-L86",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b65787f130730962df3273dfe7ccc43a720458b3a8c05dbff2abd9b64b3d397a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/%5BtaskId%5D/stop-sandbox/route.ts#L36-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f83d2ffa5dcf3dbcbeeddb73bc3c0935ed82ad9bf7ef687ba9dfdc9e85db1902:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/route.ts#L674-L727",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:499034d7603b0e97c5e984f41bfd44f21610de8d4a197b66babbf066eb9cbdea:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/git.ts#L75-L100",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cffe7a31b654303c1a3e63ffa3c025ef92e755cb752dc1b15ece5e3042d36cff:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3ab4b477ce6e4e9f8955d118e16c7724",
      "statement": "`killSandbox(taskId)` falls back to killing the oldest entry in the in-memory registry when no entry exists for the given taskId; this handles \"Try Again\" cases where a new task id is created while the old sandbox is still registered.",
